# Python Virtual Environment

Always use a virtual environment for Python scripts and tools in this project.

## Setup

If a `.venv` directory does not already exist at the project root, create one:

```bash
python3.12 -m venv .venv
```

## Activation

Before running `pip install`, `python`, or any Python command, activate the venv:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

## Installing dependencies

Always install into the venv, never globally:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate && pip install <package>
```

## Running scripts

Always run Python scripts through the venv interpreter:

```bash
.venv/bin/python script.py
# or
source .venv/bin/activate && python script.py
```
